{"body":"Records area of the M6 codebase renovation, governed by #339/#346 and docs/reviews/plan-for-the-plan.md §§5–8. The user asked, “Can we continue with our work across the various lanes?” T44 completion is verified at #691 comment6592382782; T46 #693 is next and last in the source-reading order.\n\nCurrent work: the coordinator is proving docs/reviews/briefs/records.md before explicit execution dispatch. T3 supplies the new immutable metadata transition; P1 supplies finite direct reader routes; T1 supplies the accepted T39 ownership bridge; T5 will perform the unfamiliar-executor brief proof. These are bounded preparation, not parallel audit stages.\n\nSource cutoff: d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a, tree b3ce6c6ea70d9d40ff2b74fff691a0a11f70e437. Current metadata selects127469 records paths/2190843187 logical blob bytes; the stored survey126149 rows/22984582 lines remains historical. Generated CODE totals are not a reading budget. Review records where they can mislead a current reader, with explicit line-range coverage; table the rest by folder. No deletion, relocation, historical transcript rewrite or disk-savings claim is selected.\n\nAccepted T39 corrections remain accepted but are absent from this coordinator source snapshot; #686/#807/#346 own their actual integration. #1407 remains the separate M6 backlog for nested monthly indexes and individual review of33 references/2770 lines. Separate accepted branch records do not create a merged source tree. Root owns scope, brief, criteria, outcomes, final acceptance and ordered integration.\n\nCan this be done on the VM? This work is immutable record/metadata analysis and new host record-check validation; no runtime behavior or removal proof is proposed. No build, guest, provider, host capacity, device or cloud action is authorized.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] #693 has a proved immutable ten-section brief, exact source/seed/worktree dispatch and current agent-verifiable criteria; kickoff futro and unfamiliar-executor corrections are retained.\n- [ ] #693's named audit artifacts, finite route/range coverage, folder totals and genuine Phase7 outcomes pass the applicable record lints; root acceptance and verified completion marker retain source and historical-evidence limitations.\n- [ ] Actual ordered records integration preserves historical bytes and whole ledger entries, passes new integration/record gates, and is recorded separately from simulated integration before #693 and this epic close.\n\n#693 is the child slice. Backlog #1407 remains separately scheduled; no extra audit or cleanup is created to occupy a lane.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOMM7sFc8AAAABiY3Wdg","author":{"login":"blitterbot"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"# Futro: records area #1415, T46 #693 kickoff\n\nPrepared by the M6 coordinator, Codex/GPT-6-Astra/xhigh (observed harness,\nnot provider-attested), 2026-11-03. Inputs: full #693 thread, plan §§5–8,\nthe records brief, three bounded preparation returns and the accepted T44\nretro at f01abd480f4e0b337a9fcdde2cec9bc1746b525d:\n`docs/retros/2026-11-03-m6-es-vendored-and-data.md`. Sibling heading\nconvention was read from `2026-10-24-m6-doctrine.md`. This precedes audit\nexecution; preparatory readers did not mutate the reviewed scope.\n\n## 1. What do we know and what are we assuming?\n\nT46 examines whether a finite current entrypoint sends a reader to\nmisleading records, and tables the remaining population. It is not a\nsemantic re-audit of historical QA programs. Source cutoff d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a\nwas verified by `git log -1 --format='%H %s'`:\n`d707c82ab8c48b674acc1f95a9571f0cb24d226a M6: verify T44 completion and record the next boundary (#691)`.\n\nPrimary evidence is under `docs/qa-logs/2026-11-03-m6-records-preparation/`.\nNew root metadata comparison independently agrees with T3 on127469 paths,\n2190843187 logical bytes and799/0/4 transition. Exact commands/output\nhashes and root tree are in root-metadata-verification.json. New root\nT39 comparison agrees on192 immutable identities across48 paths: all\ncandidate identities are pre-correction, all accepted/completion pairs\nmatch. Their accepted fixes remain integration-pending, not reopened.\n\nP1's five deterministic metadata outputs reproduced byte-equal under a\nnew root read. The canonical selector join yields95 occurrences/89 targets\n(88 blobs/one directory), including86 historical day logs. The original\nP1 report's missing-selector qualification remains historical; root's\nreader-routes.json records the supplied selectors and separate join.\n\nSubstrate: Git immutable objects, Python, current record tools and tracker\naccess exist and were exercised by these bounded reads. tool-help.json\nretains actual interfaces and failures: several tools do not support\n--help, and sandboxed GitHub reads failed. Source usage gives their real\nflags; future tracker-dependent checks require a distinct authorized\nnetwork attempt, not a fabricated PASS. The new worktree is prospective,\ncreated only after proof. No runtime surface is assumed.\n\nThis coordinator tree is not integrated next. Read rules from the newer\nM6 seed without merging unrelated branches. D-WORKFLOW-236 is a new\ncoordinator decision after the local register's235; accepted branch\noutcomes retain their prior IDs. No build-versus-adopt decision applies:\nthis is documentary review using existing Git and audit tools.\n\n## 2. What known unknowns need investigation?\n\n- Whether the finite routes mislead today is the audit's question, not\n  the preparation's verdict. Absent generated outputs, retired examples,\n  thirteen unresolved evidence shorthands and masked occurrences remain\n  explicit cases; a filename's absence does not decide a defect.\n- Actual disk/pack cost, reclaimable bytes, readership, runtime effects\n  and final integrated membership are unmeasured. Proceed with logical\n  metadata and named ranges; do not propose deletion or claim savings.\n- T5 must prove the v1 handoff from its literal block and check the finite\n  reading method, helper's tree predicate and scope controls. Corrections\n  enter the final brief before execution, not as later waived criteria.\n\n## 3. What patterns from prior work apply that we haven't named?\n\nT44's accepted retro names immutable program versions, snapshot-only\nchecks, missing historical receipt metadata, read-only parallel identity\noperations and unsupported cleanup custody. Therefore this brief binds\nnew program/input/output versions, distinguishes source cutoff from seed,\nchecks every commit for scope and retains unsupported scratch. Do not\nreplay old producers to make their evidence look current.\n\nT39's accepted48-path correction is not in the cutoff. The ownership\nbridge prevents duplicate work. D223/D224 and #1407 already own the\nmonthly index and33-reference follow-up; low inbound links do not imply\nnon-use. Historical work logs preserve the instructions in force then.\n\n## 4. What could we be missing?\n\nFresh-executor simulation: starting from #693's old generated15-million\nread-line count would waste the session reading QA dumps as product code.\nThe brief replaces that interpretation with ten folder rows and exact\nreader ranges. A second executor could read HEAD and count its own new\naudit recursively: bind the full source root and keep seed/output separate.\n\nA reader could treat all2.86MB of linked day logs as newly reviewed or\nrun a historical command. The brief specifies title/date, heading alignment\nand last dated entry only, with masked/unread ranges labelled. The source\nbinding helper refuses an extra empty subtree, not just leaf drift.\n\nPremortem: the table reports savings and deletes repeated evidence, or\nfiles T39's accepted correction as new work. Seven new audit-local\nrefusals cover missing/duplicate keys, invented reading/currency/cost and\nownership claims; no cleanup/removal authorization exists in A–D.\n\nBlindspots13/47/51/75 apply to evidence, source versus installed context,\nstale checklist state and wrong-tree reading. No mechanism is replaced;\nno old guard/citation may be dropped as part of this table. If the audit\nfinds a real current defect, a stream brief owns the later edit and proof.\n\n## 5. What adjustments or investigations must happen BEFORE execution?\n\n1. Keep D236 and the ten-section brief/source helper together; preserve\n   preparation reports and root checks without changing historical reports.\n2. Complete the unfamiliar-executor proof, record concrete errata and\n   publish the final brief/criteria. No audit execution on v1 alone.\n3. Verify actual #1415→#693 parent relation, M6 placement, new worktree,\n   clean exact seed and explicit T3 A–D dispatch. Root keeps acceptance.\n4. Update milestone and continuity with observed lane work, not prompt\n   delivery alone. Available support lanes remain available without\n   duplicate audit work. All record subprocesses stay on CPUs8–23.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-03T11:34:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/pixelelated/distribution/issues/1415#issuecomment-6602741366","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":1415,"state":"OPEN","title":"M6.P2: Records provenance and reader guidance"}
